-- SEO: bold 1-3 keyword phrases in every SG course overview and category description (user directive
-- 2026-10-30: "bold some of the keywords in the course description or catalog description").
--
-- Phrases come from each page's own name + meta keywords (primary keyword first, e.g. the course/category
-- name, then specific tools/skills such as "OpenClaw", "agile project management"). Rules:
--   * course overview (short_description): only the INTRO paragraphs before the first heading/div/table/hr,
--     because view.phtml regex-carves the later Funding / Learning Outcomes / Brochure / vendor sections;
--   * category description: only <p>/<li> text, never the p.category-image banner;
--   * never inside a link, heading or existing bold; never a funding term; first occurrence only; whole words;
--   * rows that already carry 2+ bold tags are skipped.
-- The 17 keyword landing categories (1877 + 1878) are excluded - their copy carries its own bolding.
--
-- Each UPDATE only INSERTs '<strong>' / '</strong>' at fixed character positions and is guarded by
-- MD5(value) of the exact live text it was generated from (SG prod, 2026-10-30), so a description edited
-- since then is skipped untouched (peer-safe), and a re-run is a no-op. Verified read-only against SG prod:
-- 968/968 rows matched and MD5(result) equals the expected new text for every row.
-- SG-only (@sg guard; MD5 + ids also never match a partner DB). Post-deploy: catalog_category_flat +
-- catalog_product_flat reindex + cache flush.

SET @sg := (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM core_store WHERE store_id = 1 AND code = 'singapore');
